      "cr": 0.125,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Waluipedia cast sheet — Times New Roman.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-character-sheets.py</code>, generated from the article's own words. XP ledger: level 1, power rating 2 → CR 1/8 as a scholar. Numbers are a GM-ready reading of the record, not a filed stat line; the article stays the authority. Archive date 1040 BF.</p><p><strong>The Family Typesetter</strong> — Snowdin Chronicle Office</p><p>Status: Active — recorded in the Snowdin household registry</p><p>A formal historian who believes every family story deserves dates, sources, and a respectable typeface. Times New Roman documents Bone-Line events in a carefully indexed chronicle and distrusts any story introduced with “you had to be there.” His severe presentation conceals a deep affection for embarrassing childhood anecdotes.</p><h3>Evidence</h3><ul><li><strong>Dagger</strong> — “The Family Typesetter”</li><li><strong>Keen Records</strong> — “Behind the severity is an archivist who cannot resist a good embarrassing childhood story.”</li><li><strong>Cooks for an Army</strong> — “The chronicle's least formal pages record who cried at which puzzle, whose first spaghetti attempt was structurally unsound, and exactly when Sans's puns became a household hazard.”</li><li><strong>Puzzle Discipline</strong> — “The chronicle's least formal pages record who cried at which puzzle, whose first spaghetti attempt was structurally unsound, and exactly when Sans's puns became a household hazard.”</li></ul><p>Article: <code>#/article/times_new_roman</code> (characters). Site sheet: <code>#/sheets/times_new_roman</code>.</p>",
        "public": ""
      },
